## Interview explanation

“On Day 23, I implemented a controlled manual-review resolution workflow for transactions whose results could not be confirmed through automatic reconciliation. I added pessimistic row locking to prevent concurrent conflicting decisions, restricted final outcomes to completed or failed, required an operations reason, and executed the status update and audit-history insertion in one database transaction. I also added validation, duplicate-resolution protection, Swagger documentation, and unit tests.”